  {
   "t": "notice",
   "text": "Draft for Jared’s approval. Figures are closed sales from Jared’s Paragon export; the neighbourhood map outlines are drawn by us and stay draft until each is confirmed.",
   "gen": "gvr"
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "text": "Vancouver is split into 41 MLS® sub-areas, the neighbourhood boundaries the Greater Vancouver REALTORS® board uses for every listing and sale. From November 2025 to October 22, 2026, 5,697 homes sold across them: 1,243 houses, 3,241 condos and 597 townhomes and 613 duplexes. The busiest were Downtown (467), Kitsilano (425), Yaletown (335).",
   "gen": "gvr"
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "text": "By median price, the houses that sold in Shaughnessy were the most expensive of the 28 Vancouver neighbourhoods with 10 or more house sales ($4,817,500), and those in Collingwood the least ($1,510,000). For condos, the range ran from $520,000 in Collingwood to $1,228,000 in Coal Harbour.",
   "gen": "gvr"
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "text": "These are MLS® sub-areas, not the City of Vancouver’s planning areas, so a neighbourhood here can be larger or smaller than the name suggests. The map and tables below follow the board’s boundaries. Use them to compare areas, then ask Jared for a search set to the exact streets you care about.",
   "gen": "gvr"
  },
